  "description": "Erection of a single storey side extension, conversion of roof space to habitable including the installation of five side-facing rooflights, hip-to-gable roof alteration with a new rear gable window, and installation of pitched roofs over the porch and side extension.",
  "development_type": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed roof extension by reason of its bulk, form, design, depth, size and siting would be overly large and fail to harmonise with the existing character of the dwelling. The proposed roof alterations on the side and front porch by reason of their design would also fail to harmonise the existing character of the dwelling. The side element bu reason of its depth would not be an acceptable addition given its sitting and form. The roof element would fail to read as subservient additions, subsequently failing to preserve or enhance the character and appearance of the streetscene of Conservation area, all contrary to the NPPF (2024), Policy BE1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part One Strategic Policies (2012) and Policies DMHD 1, DMHB 4 and DMHB 11 of of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part Two - Development Management Policies (2020).",
    "The proposed roof and side extension, by virtue of its height, bulk, form, depth, size, siting and proximity, would be perceived to be detrimental to the amenities of the neighbouring occupiers, by reason of overdominance. Therefore the proposal would be contrary to Policies BE1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan: Part One - Strategic Policies (November 2012), Policies DMHB 11 and DMHD 1 of the Hillingdon Local Plan Part Two - Development Management Policies (January 2020).",
    "The decision to REFUSE planning permission has been taken having regard to all relevant planning legislation, regulations, guidance, circulars and Council policies, including The Human Rights Act (1998) (HRA 1998) which makes it unlawful for the Council to act incompatibly with Convention rights, specifically Article 6 (right to a fair hearing); Article 8 (right to respect for private and family life); Article 1 of the First Protocol (protection of property) and Article 14 (prohibition of discrimination).",
    "The decision to REFUSE planning permission has been taken having regard to the policies and proposals in the Hillingdon Local Plan Part 1 (2012) and Part 2 (2020) set out below, including Supplementary Planning Guidance, and to all relevant material considerations, including The London Plan (2021) and national guidance."
  ],
